    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10774" root="خصر" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْصَرُ</span></b>  [<i>Shorter:</i> and <i>shortest</i>]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْصَرُ مِنْ ذَاكَ</span> <i>This</i> [road] <i>is shorter than that.</i>
(A.) But this is irregular; <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْصَرُ</span> being formed
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُخْتُصِرَ</span>, a verb of more than three letters.
(I' Ak p. 237.)

